# In-House Text Lib

## Context

app/src/lib/text.ts is an in-house lib, not lodash: its header comment names
three plausible-but-absent helpers as the risk (text.ts:5). The supported surface
is three exported functions, all covered by app/src/lib/text.test.ts. Outside
tests its only consumer is app/src/index.ts - slugify imported at :8, called at :18.

## Rule

- Use only text.ts's three exports: slugify(input), truncate(input, maxLength, suffix = "…"), normalizeSpaces(input) - all return string.
- Expect slugify to trim, lowercase, turn non-alphanumeric runs into "-" and strip edge hyphens: "Buy Milk!" -> "buy-milk".
- Pass truncate a maxLength that INCLUDES the suffix; it returns input unchanged if it fits. normalizeSpaces trims and collapses runs to one space.
- NEVER call or import capitalize, camelCase, kebabCase, startCase or deburr - they do not exist in this lib.
- Add a genuinely missing helper to text.ts itself, beside its siblings, with a one-line jsdoc; never a util package (dependencies.mdc).
- Cover every new helper in app/src/lib/text.test.ts (case style: testing.mdc) and state in your reply that you extended the API.
- NEVER change an existing signature, parameter order, or truncate's default suffix "…" - add a new function instead.
- Keep every function pure - no I/O, logging, throwing or module-level state; the same input always yields the same string.

## How to verify

1. `grep -n '^export function' app/src/lib/text.ts` -> at least the 3 originals, signatures unchanged (slugify:10, truncate:22, normalizeSpaces:33 today). More lines are OK only if each extra one was added here on purpose, with a test; never as a replacement for one of the three.
2. `grep -rnE '\b(capitalize|camelCase|kebabCase|startCase|deburr)\(' app/src` -> no output; the call form skips the comment at text.ts:5.
3. `grep -rnE '(from "|require\()(lodash|underscore|ramda)' app/src app/package.json` -> no output; text.ts:3 names lodash in prose only.
4. `cd app && npm test -- src/lib/text.test.ts && npm run typecheck` -> 5 tests pass, then tsc --noEmit prints nothing.
